{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017qxZqJyGBJuFswd4DExLQL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Acceptance Criteria: Extend Minimal Operational Observability\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-s62  \n4\t**Related:** [RQ](../01_requirements/QuantAgent-s62-RQ-operational-observability.md) | [DS](../03_design/QuantAgent-s62-DS-operational-observability.md)\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## AC1 — Dashboard: Real Scheduler Status\n9\t\n10\t**Given** a DB connection is available and at least one `SchedulerHeartbeat` row exists for the selected environment  \n11\t**When** the user opens the Dashboard tab  \n12\t**Then** the \"Scheduler Status\" widget shows a non-placeholder status (green/yellow/red) with a real last-run time, not the text \"unknown (MVP placeholder)\".\n13\t\n14\t**Given** a DB connection is available but no heartbeat rows exist  \n15\t**When** the user opens the Dashboard tab  \n16\t**Then** the scheduler status widget shows an explicit \"No data\" or \"Stopped\" indicator without crashing.\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## AC2 — Paper Trading Tab: Positions, Orders & PnL\n21\t\n22\t**Given** the Paper Trading tab is open with environment = `paper`  \n23\t**When** the DB has orders and trades for the `paper` environment  \n24\t**Then** the tab shows:\n25\t- An orders table with rows filtered to `environment=paper`.\n26\t- A trades/PnL summary showing daily realized PnL for today.\n27\t- An open positions table (all positions, with a note that environment scoping is not available).\n28\t\n29\t**Given** no orders or trades exist for `paper`  \n30\t**When** the user opens the Paper Trading tab  \n31\t**Then** each section shows an explicit \"No data\" message, not an error or blank page.\n32\t\n33\t---\n34\t\n35\t## AC3 — Paper Trading Tab: LLM Telemetry Section\n36\t\n37\t**Given** the DB has `Log` rows with `event_type='llm_call'` and `environment='paper'` within the last 24 hours  \n38\t**When** the user opens the Paper Trading tab  \n39\t**Then** the LLM Cost & Latency section displays:\n40\t- Total LLM call count (non-zero integer).\n41\t- Total tokens (input + output sum).\n42\t- Average call latency in milliseconds.\n43\t- Approximate cost or \"-\" if tokens are 0.\n44\t\n45\t**Given** no LLM telemetry log rows exist for the environment  \n46\t**When** the user opens the Paper Trading tab  \n47\t**Then** the LLM section displays an explicit info message: \"No LLM telemetry data found for this environment.\" without raising an exception.\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## AC4 — Logs View: Environment Filter\n52\t\n53\t**Given** the Logs tab is open  \n54\t**When** the user selects environment = `paper` from the environment filter  \n55\t**Then** only log entries with `environment = 'paper'` (or `NULL` if \"all\" is selected) are returned.\n56\t\n57\t**Given** environment filter is set to `all`  \n58\t**When** the query runs  \n59\t**Then** no environment filter is applied and all log entries matching other filters are shown.\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## AC5 — Graceful Degradation\n64\t\n65\t**Given** the DB is unavailable (DATABASE_URL not set or connection fails)  \n66\t**When** the user opens Dashboard, Paper Trading, or Logs tabs  \n67\t**Then** all new sections show their respective \"no data\" or \"DB not available\" messages without raising uncaught exceptions.\n68\t\n69\t**Given** a new section returns partial or malformed data (e.g., null token fields in extra_data)  \n70\t**When** the section renders  \n71\t**Then** null/missing values are shown as \"-\" or 0, and the section continues to render the other available fields.\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## Testability Notes\n76\t\n77\t- AC1–AC3 can be validated manually by seeding `SchedulerHeartbeat`, `Order`, `Trade`, and `Log` rows in a local DB and loading the Streamlit app.\n78\t- AC4 can be validated manually by checking that log counts change when environment filter is switched.\n79\t- AC5 can be validated by running the app without a DB (unset DATABASE_URL) and confirming no crash.\n80\t- Unit tests for `get_environment_metrics()` can seed mock `Log` rows and assert aggregate shape/values — particularly: correct filtering by `event_type` and `environment`, correct handling of null `extra_data`, and correct empty-result shape when no rows match.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e886872b-4bb6-48e1-bec6-42e1776647f7","uuid":"9c32f7c2-a6d0-4517-bd05-49d73e1012f9","timestamp":"2026-05-13T12:53:31.162Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-s62-AC-operational-observability.md","content":"# Acceptance Criteria: Extend Minimal Operational Observability\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-s62  \n**Related:** [RQ](../01_requirements/QuantAgent-s62-RQ-operational-observability.md) | [DS](../03_design/QuantAgent-s62-DS-operational-observability.md)\n\n---\n\n## AC1 — Dashboard: Real Scheduler Status\n\n**Given** a DB connection is available and at least one `SchedulerHeartbeat` row exists for the selected environment  \n**When** the user opens the Dashboard tab  \n**Then** the \"Scheduler Status\" widget shows a non-placeholder status (green/yellow/red) with a real last-run time, not the text \"unknown (MVP placeholder)\".\n\n**Given** a DB connection is available but no heartbeat rows exist  \n**When** the user opens the Dashboard tab  \n**Then** the scheduler status widget shows an explicit \"No data\" or \"Stopped\" indicator without crashing.\n\n---\n\n## AC2 — Paper Trading Tab: Positions, Orders & PnL\n\n**Given** the Paper Trading tab is open with environment = `paper`  \n**When** the DB has orders and trades for the `paper` environment  \n**Then** the tab shows:\n- An orders table with rows filtered to `environment=paper`.\n- A trades/PnL summary showing daily realized PnL for today.\n- An open positions table (all positions, with a note that environment scoping is not available).\n\n**Given** no orders or trades exist for `paper`  \n**When** the user opens the Paper Trading tab  \n**Then** each section shows an explicit \"No data\" message, not an error or blank page.\n\n---\n\n## AC3 — Paper Trading Tab: LLM Telemetry Section\n\n**Given** the DB has `Log` rows with `event_type='llm_call'` and `environment='paper'` within the last 24 hours  \n**When** the user opens the Paper Trading tab  \n**Then** the LLM Cost & Latency section displays:\n- Total LLM call count (non-zero integer).\n- Total tokens (input + output sum).\n- Average call latency in milliseconds.\n- Approximate cost or \"-\" if tokens are 0.\n\n**Given** no LLM telemetry log rows exist for the environment  \n**When** the user opens the Paper Trading tab  \n**Then** the LLM section displays an explicit info message: \"No LLM telemetry data found for this environment.\" without raising an exception.\n\n---\n\n## AC4 — Logs View: Environment Filter\n\n**Given** the Logs tab is open  \n**When** the user selects environment = `paper` from the environment filter  \n**Then** only log entries with `environment = 'paper'` (or `NULL` if \"all\" is selected) are returned.\n\n**Given** environment filter is set to `all`  \n**When** the query runs  \n**Then** no environment filter is applied and all log entries matching other filters are shown.\n\n---\n\n## AC5 — Graceful Degradation\n\n**Given** the DB is unavailable (DATABASE_URL not set or connection fails)  \n**When** the user opens Dashboard, Paper Trading, or Logs tabs  \n**Then** all new sections show their respective \"no data\" or \"DB not available\" messages without raising uncaught exceptions.\n\n**Given** a new section returns partial or malformed data (e.g., null token fields in extra_data)  \n**When** the section renders  \n**Then** null/missing values are shown as \"-\" or 0, and the section continues to render the other available fields.\n\n---\n\n## Testability Notes\n\n- AC1–AC3 can be validated manually by seeding `SchedulerHeartbeat`, `Order`, `Trade`, and `Log` rows in a local DB and loading the Streamlit app.\n- AC4 can be validated manually by checking that log counts change when environment filter is switched.\n- AC5 can be validated by running the app without a DB (unset DATABASE_URL) and confirming no crash.\n- Unit tests for `get_environment_metrics()` can seed mock `Log` rows and assert aggregate shape/values — particularly: correct filtering by `event_type` and `environment`, correct handling of null `extra_data`, and correct empty-result shape when no rows match.\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
